    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-047 — CSS mask-image.** Three commits on one branch, merged after Commit 2's PNG verification.\n\nCloses ADR-045's mask-image deferral. 14 renderable rule combinations in Wikipedia CSS (mask + background-color fill). Primary first-viewport target: `.cdx-message__icon` (issue-box icon).\n\n## Commits\n\n| # | Scope | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Parse + layout fields** (behavior-neutral) | ✅ Green — 598 / 2307 tests pass, +12 new |\n| 2 | **Paint** (visible: masked icons) | ⏳ Pending — PNG verification before merge |\n| 3 | **Docs** (ADR-047 → Implemented) | ⏳ Pending |\n\n## Commit 1 details\n\n### What shipped\n\n- `LayoutBox` gains 7 mask fields (`mask_image_url`, `mask_size_w/h`, `mask_pos_x/y`, `mask_no_repeat`, `mask_has`)\n- `BgPosX`/`BgPosY` enums moved above `LayoutBox` (were below, before `LineFragment`; mask fields need them at declaration site — a compile-order fix)\n- Parse `mask-image` / `-webkit-mask-image` (URL + data URL forms)\n- Parse `mask-size` (fixed length; auto/cover/contain/percentage deferred)\n- Parse `mask-position` (keyword pairs, flexible order)\n- Parse `mask-repeat` (no-repeat only)\n- `mask-image: none` clears `mask_has`\n\n### Two bugs caught by unit tests before commit\n\n**1. Use-after-free (SIGSEGV)**\n```cpp\n// Initial draft:\nauto mask_lookup = [&](...) -> const std::string* {\n    if (auto v = style->get(unprefixed); v) return &*v;\n    //                                              ^^^^\n    // v is a temporary optional<string>. &*v points\n    // into memory destroyed when lambda returns.\n};\n```\nUnit test crashed immediately. Fixed by returning `std::string` **by value** (owning copy, one small-string copy per parse — negligible).\n\n**2. String-replace collision**\n`for (char c : *ps)` → `for (char c : ps)` replacement hit `apply_inline_bg_pp`'s loop (ADR-045, where `ps` is `std::optional<string>` and needs `*ps`) instead of the mask block (where `ps` is `std::string` by value). Fixed with context-scoped replacement.\n\nBoth bugs were caught before commit — the session's \"verify before committing\" discipline paying off.\n\n## Commit 2 preview (visible delta)\n\n- New `paint_mask_image()` using `cairo_mask_surface`\n- `paint_box` calls it after background fill, before border\n- **PNG verification gate before merge**\n- Primary target: `.cdx-message__icon` (first-viewport issue-box icon)\n- Header icons may appear once ADR-029 completes\n\n## Deferred (per ADR)\n\n- `mask-mode: luminance`\n- `mask-composite`, `mask-border`, `mask-clip`, `mask-origin`\n- Percentage `mask-size` / `mask-position`\n- `mask-repeat: repeat | repeat-x | repeat-y`\n- Elements with mask but no `background-color` fill\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before ADR-047: 586 cases / 2263 assertions\n- After Commit 1: **598 cases / 2307 assertions** (+12 / +44)\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Return-by-value in mask_lookup** — the initial pointer-into-optional draft was a use-after-free (SIGSEGV on first parse). Fixed before commit. Cost: one small-string copy per mask parse.\n- [ ] **`cairo_mask_surface` plan for Commit 2** — mask the current source (bg-color) through surface alpha. Single Cairo call, exact CSS semantics.\n- [ ] **v1 renders only when `background_color.a > 0`** — transparent bg + mask = invisible mask anyway, so skip. Zero visual artifact. 14 target rules all have bg-color.\n- [ ] **`-webkit-mask-*` prefixes accepted** — many Wikipedia rules set both for browser compat. Unprefixed wins if both present.\n- [ ] **Honest scope: 3 of 4 targets header-dependent** — only `.cdx-message__icon` guaranteed first-viewport. If that element doesn't render, delta is 0 (infrastructure still correct). Documented.\n\n## DO NOT MERGE until Commit 2's PNG verification passes.\n\nRefs #224\n",
